# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5). L §5.19: "After the reading's pad or anchor has set the total, a stated
# part is q's balance, as a stated total is the place's. Where it differs from q's booked part, the difference is q's own
# gap: where positive, a part of q's of that amount, from the reading's document; where negative, a take of q's parts by
# the leaving rule, its terms on w holes as above. The unstated rest has a gap of its own, over the labels the reading
# doesn't state". The start pad takes 30.00 of ania's 100.00 (no other movement that day); ania's stated 60.00 is a gap
# of -10.00, a take of ania's; the rest, 10.00 over no booked part, is a hole part that can't be ania's: so tomek's is
# HOLE-PART (scratch/expfix1.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == tomek then 0 else 1
kind tomeks: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-01), bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-01) of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-03-02
  pad konto from world
  stated[konto] = 70.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start
  stated[konto] of ania = 60.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start
=== expect
q: (70.00 PLN, 60.00 PLN, ?"konto: 10.00 PLN may be tomek's: whose are 10.00 PLN of konto at 2026-03-01 start?" (konto))
  pad: konto 2026-03-01 start, pads:stmt:konto@2026-03-01 start of -30.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-01
